<BlogLayout 
  title="How to Find Your Perfect Bralette Fit" 
  description="A complete guide to measuring, sizing, and choosing the right bralette for your body type."
  pubDate="2026-06-01"
  tags={['Fit Guide', 'Bralette', 'Sizing']}
>
  <p>Finding the perfect bralette shouldn't be complicated. Here's everything you need to know about getting the right fit.</p>
  
  <h2>Measure Yourself Correctly</h2>
  <p>Start with a soft measuring tape. Measure around your rib cage, just under your bust — that's your band size. Then measure around the fullest part of your bust. The difference between these two measurements helps determine your cup size.</p>
  
  <h2>Know Your Style</h2>
  <p>Bralettes come in many styles — triangle, plunge, bandeau, longline. Each offers different coverage and support. Triangle bralettes are great for smaller busts, while longline styles offer more structure for fuller figures.</p>
  
  <h2>Material Matters</h2>
  <p>Lace bralettes are romantic and breathable, but look for ones with a soft lining. Cotton blends are perfect for everyday wear. For sleep, opt for seamless modal or bamboo fabrics.</p>

  <h2>Our Sizing Tip</h2>
  <p>At Charlizi, most of our bralettes are sized S/M/L rather than traditional band/cup sizes. If you're between sizes, go up for a more relaxed fit or down if you prefer more support.</p>
</BlogLayout>
